### Phase 3B — feed, detail, my items
@host = http://localhost:8080
@token = paste-user-access-token-here
@postId = 1

### 1. Feed, defaults  -> 200, data.size == 12, page == 0
GET {{host}}/api/posts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2. Feed with every filter  -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/posts?category=1&type=SELL&q=textbook&minPrice=100&maxPrice=1000&sort=priceAsc&page=0&size=5
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3. Wildcards in q are literal  -> 200, no 500 (escape check)
GET {{host}}/api/posts?q=50%25_off
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. size above the cap  -> 200, data.size == 50
GET {{host}}/api/posts?size=999
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. Invalid sort  -> 400
GET {{host}}/api/posts?sort=cheapest
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. Invalid enum for type  -> 400
GET {{host}}/api/posts?type=RENT
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. Feed without a token  -> 401
GET {{host}}/api/posts

### 8. Detail of an approved same-college post  -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/posts/{{postId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9. Detail of another college's post  -> 404 (never 403)
GET {{host}}/api/posts/999999
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 10. Non-numeric id  -> 404
GET {{host}}/api/posts/abc
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 11. My items, all statuses (DELETED excluded)  -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/posts/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 12. My rejected items include rejectionReason  -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/posts/mine?status=REJECTED
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 13. Mine with an invalid status enum  -> 400
GET {{host}}/api/posts/mine?status=NOPE
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 14. Expiry check: set a post's expires_at in the past, reload the feed
###     -> that post disappears from /api/posts and its detail becomes 404
###     for a same-college non-owner.
###     psql: update posts set expires_at = now() - interval '1 day' where id = <id>;

### 15. Non-owner sees pending  -> 404
###     Create a second user in the same college, then request a PENDING_REVIEW
###     post id created by the first user.